infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Union vs intersection — one-of and all-of are opposites
  desc Mirror-image behaviour on members, calling, value sets, and never
  compares
    - label Union A | B — one-of
      children
        - label Value is either A or B
          desc Which one is undecided statically, until you narrow
        - label Reachable: common members only
          desc Touch only what every member has; one-sided fields need narrowing
        - label Easy to provide
          desc A part fits the whole-or: number is assignable to number | string
        - label Wider value set
          desc The union of both sets — more values qualify
        - label Disjoint primitives stay usable
          desc "on" | "off" is a fine two-member union, nothing collapses
    - label Intersection A & B — all-of
      children
        - label Value is A and B at once
          desc It satisfies both contracts, so every member is guaranteed
        - label Reachable: every member of both
          desc For objects, & merges all properties of both sides
        - label Hard to provide
          desc The whole-and demands everything; a partial object is rejected
        - label Narrower value set
          desc Fewer values qualify, yet each one carries more fields
        - label Disjoint primitives become never
          desc string & number = never silently; the error surfaces only on use
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
